# --- docs/ is intentionally NOT listed here (tried, then reverted — see
# graphify-improvements.md "Scope-fix + refresh" for the full story). A
# .graphifyignore does not scope to "only this detect_incremental() call": it
# cascades by filesystem ancestry, from the nearest VCS root down to whatever
# scan root is passed in (graphify.detect._load_graphifyignore). Repo root is
# an ancestor of BOTH scan roots this project uses ('.' and 'docs'), so any
# rule written here is loaded for a docs-rooted scan too — verified the hard
# way: a `docs/` line here collapsed detect_incremental(root='docs')'s real
# 51-changed-document baseline to 0 (every doc under docs/ matched and was
# excluded, not just the intended root-scope noise). Reverted before this
# file was ever used for an actual extract/merge.
#
# The real hazard this was trying to prevent is still real and still avoided,
# just at the call-site instead of the ignore-file: a root-rooted
# detect_incremental('.') cannot safely diff against the docs-rooted manifest
# (graphify.detect.load_manifest(path, root=<given root>) re-anchors every
# stored relative key, e.g. "ANALYSIS-v149.md", against WHATEVER root is
# passed in — with root='.' that resolves to a file that does not exist, so
# every one of the ~163 already-tracked docs reports as BOTH "changed" AND
# "deleted"). Verified empirically: detect_incremental(".") reports
# deleted_files=163, 100% phantom (0 real deletions).
#
# Fix: the refresh procedure only ever reads the 'code' category out of a
# root-rooted detect_incremental() result, and never its 'document'/'image'
# categories or its deleted_files list — those come exclusively from the
# separate, correctly-rooted detect_incremental(root='docs') call (established
# flow, graphify-improvements.md §4). See "Scope-fix + refresh" for the
# before/after counts this produced.

